To raise the timeout for a single test, you can use `test.setTimeout()` or `test.slow()`:

*   **`test.setTimeout(120_000)`**: Sets a specific timeout (e.g., 120,000ms).
*   **`test.slow()`**: An easy way to triple the default timeout.

Example:
```typescript
test('very slow test', async ({ page }) => {
  test.setTimeout(120_000);
  // ...
});

test('slow test', async ({ page }) => {
  test.slow();
  // ...
});
```

